From 9ebc02df2040c4845a631dd08e2c95dc94e6a3d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: M0n7y5 <17201053+M0n7y5@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 11:16:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] winepipewire.drv: Drop the oldest capture packet when the
 list is full.

When the application stops collecting, the packet free list empties and the
timer thread has to overwrite a packet that is still waiting to be read.  It
recycled the oldest and marked the successor, except when the oldest already
carried a discontinuity, in which case it overwrote the newest packet instead
and marked nothing.

That branch discards the freshest audio, keeps the stale backlog, and leaves
the gap invisible: the application is handed old audio followed by a much
later packet with nothing to say the two are not adjacent.  It also clears a
discontinuity the application has not read yet.

Always recycle the oldest and always move the flag to its successor.  Where
the oldest already carried a flag, the gap it described merges with the new
one and the successor's flag covers both.  The free list is empty on this
path, so the successor always exists.

Driven with a wpw_capoverrun mode that starves the application rather than the
ring, which is what empties the free list: 21 unflagged gaps per run before
this on both arches, none after.

Inherited from winepulse, which has the same branch at pulse.c:1643-1647.
---
 dlls/winepipewire.drv/pipewire.c | 15 ++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winepipewire.drv/pipewire.c b/dlls/winepipewire.drv/pipewire.c
index 347ec59038a..d07e1d13034 100644
--- a/dlls/winepipewire.drv/pipewire.c
+++ b/dlls/winepipewire.drv/pipewire.c
@@ -2428,13 +2428,14 @@ static void pipewire_read(struct pipewire_stream *stream)
                 __atomic_store_n(&slot->word, CAP_WORD(seq, CAP_FULL), __ATOMIC_RELEASE);
                 return;
             }
-            if (!p->discont)
-            {
-                next = (ACPacket *)p->entry.next;
-                next->discont = 1;
-            }
-            else
-                p = (ACPacket *)list_tail(&stream->packet_filled_head);
+            /* Recycle the oldest packet, matching the ring below, and move
+             * the discontinuity onto its successor, which is the packet that
+             * gaps.  Recycling the newest instead would discard the freshest
+             * audio, leave the gap unmarked and clear a flag the application
+             * has not read.  The free list is empty here, so the successor
+             * always exists. */
+            next = (ACPacket *)p->entry.next;
+            next->discont = 1;
         }
         else
         {
-- 
